 "desc": "A heavier, more articulate Lorna Shore rig for 8-string (low D1, upper strings in drop G). An output selector after the gate picks the path. A: a tight TS boost into a 5150III lead channel and a VH4, mud cut before the amps and a tight low shelf plus upper-mid bite after. B: a heavy, dark clean with no distortion at all, a compressor and a slow, dark chorus into a JC-120 and a Twin with the treble down and lots of headroom, so even the D1 string stays clean. Both share the ping-pong delay and the big hall.",
